<DocsPageTitle Path="Components/Collapse">
    Blazorise Collapse Component
</DocsPageTitle>

<DocsPageLead>
    Keep supporting content available without taking up space until users need it.
</DocsPageLead>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Overview
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Use the <Code>Collapse</Code> component for filter panels, additional details, and other sections that users can expand or hide. A visible header provides a place for the control that toggles the content.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Using collapsible sections helps organize information, keeping the interface clean and easy to navigate. This approach also complements accordions when you need a single collapsible block rather than multiple linked items.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Structure
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    A <Code>Collapse</Code> contains an always-visible header and a body that expands or collapses.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsAnatomy Label="Collapse component anatomy">
    <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="Collapse" Description="Manages the expanded or collapsed state.">
        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="CollapseHeader" Description="The visible header; can contain a toggle button." />
        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="CollapseBody" Description="Contains the content that expands or collapses." />
    </DocsAnatomyRegion>
</DocsAnatomy>

