<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Animation">
        <Paragraph>
            Set <Code>Animated="false"</Code> for immediate transitions, or use <Code>AnimationDuration</Code> to adjust their duration in milliseconds.
            A duration of zero or less disables transitions. Leaving the duration unset preserves the selected CSS provider's timing.
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            These settings control panel transitions where supported. Bootstrap 4 and Bootstrap 5 animate expansion and collapse, using a default duration of 350 milliseconds.
            The controls apply to this collapse; nested components keep their own settings.
        </Paragraph>
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="CollapseAnimationExample" Outlined FullWidth>
        <CollapseAnimationExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Best Practices
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageSubsectionTitle IncludeInToc="false">
    Use Clear Toggles
</DocsPageSubsectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    The header should describe the hidden content, and the intended toggle must be reachable and operable by keyboard. Keep the expanded state synchronized through one binding or event path, especially when the collapse can also be controlled programmatically.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSubsectionTitle IncludeInToc="false">
    Essential Information
</DocsPageSubsectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Do not place critical status, validation feedback, or the only way to complete a task inside content that starts collapsed. When several related collapsible sections need coordinated behavior, use an <Anchor To="docs/components/accordion">Accordion</Anchor> instead.
</DocsPageParagraph>

